## Settings

### 10. Settings surfacing gaps (todo #14) — ✔ all four fixed
- **a)** new `memory.learned` op; Settings shows memory.md inline with
  last-updated, or "Nothing learned yet". (The file had content — the old
  view was just an open-in-editor button.)
- **b)** proposed/active routine rows now show trigger phrases + numbered
  steps before Approve.
- **c)** all three rule-creation paths already wrote the same RuleStore —
  regression test added ("always label…" chat path appears in rules.list).
- **d)** Mail screen re-queries the mirror on every show, and rule saves
  refresh the list — new labels/pills appear without a restart.
- **a) "What Lumen has learned" is empty.** Either the view is broken or it
  reads the wrong store — distilled memory lives at
  `~/.local/share/lumen/memory.md`. Show its contents + last-updated time;
  if genuinely empty, say "nothing learned yet" instead of blank.
- **b) Proposed routines aren't inspectable.** Before accepting a proposed
  routine, the user must be able to see what it does — steps, schedule,
  what it touches.
- **c) Email rules don't appear in Settings.** The rules editor exists
  (`[mail_rules]`, `rule_dialog.py`) — likely rules created via the chat /
  "always label like this" paths aren't landing where the editor reads.
  All three creation paths must write the same rules table, and the editor
  must list everything in it.
- **d) Label pills aren't dynamic.** When a new label appears (created by a
  rule or an accepted suggestion), the chip row and row pills must pick it
  up on the next `emails.list` — no restart required.
